-- title:
--   Definitions for Energy-constrained diamond norms and their use in quantum information theory
-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *Energy-constrained diamond norms and their use in quantum information theory* (arXiv:1706.00361) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `diagonalEnergy`: PDF pp.6,8: spectral-cutoff energy in a Hamiltonian eigenbasis, retaining infinity. Used on positive nuclear coefficients, including actual marginals; the nonnegative series equals the supremum of bounded spectral-cutoff traces.
--   - `eigenbasisGroundEnergy`: PDF p.6: spectrum infimum for an unordered nonnegative eigenvalue list; the range is nonempty and bounded below by zero. The accepted Frontier30.P05 groundEnergy instead requires an ordered divergent EnergySpectrum.
--   - `EigenbasisGibbsCondition`: PDF p.8, (6): every positive inverse temperature has finite partition trace. In particular all spectral sublevel sets are finite. This series adapter accepts an eigenvalue list; the accepted P13.GibbsCondition instead accepts a general closed quadratic form and is used directly below.
--   - `ensembleBarycenter`: PDF p.10: coefficients of the actual trace-norm Bochner barycenter. State coordinates are bounded and trace-norm continuous, so these scalar integrals are integrable and uniquely specify that same normalized state.
--   - `ecdMagnitude`: PDF p.6, (2): full channel-difference ECD supremum, without a half. The reference is fixed, infinite-dimensional and separable. Every normalized, possibly entangled, energy-admissible state occurs. On channel differences this extended expression is finite (at most two); no real conversion is used.
--   - `siteMarginal`: PDF pp.12–13: trace out every site except k. Configurations fixed to zero at k index exactly the discarded coordinates; updating to i,j inserts the retained matrix indices. No finite-support restriction is imposed.
--   - `maxInputEnergy`: PDF p.12: computed maximum of actual input marginal energies. The empty extended supremum is zero; block statements require n>=1.
--   - `meanOutputEnergy`: PDF p.13: computed MEAN output energy, using actual input marginals.
--   - `referencedTensorOutput`: PDF pp.12–13: actual memoryless n-copy output with reference untouched. Reuse the accepted tensor power, including every off-diagonal block. Claimed50.P40.blockOutput instead constructs finite classical-input product states; it cannot evaluate arbitrary entangled inputs or an untouched reference.
--   - `blockMutualInformation`: PDF p.4, (1), and p.13: extended block QMI as relative entropy with its actual marginals, avoiding subtraction of possibly infinite entropies.
--   - `continuityRatio`: PDF p.10: r_epsilon(t), used at epsilon>0 and 0<t<=1/(2epsilon). The denominator is at least one half on this domain.
--   - `holevoBound`: PDF p.10, (12): the complete scalar Holevo continuity expression.
--   - `MajorantRegularity`: PDF pp.8–9, (9)–(10): scalar regularity of a majorant, without imposing continuity of the second derivative. Domination of F_H is irrelevant to Remark 2's scalar implication from (10).
--   - `formGroundEnergy`: PDF pp.5–6: spectral infimum via the equivalent Rayleigh infimum on the unit form domain. A nonzero separable Hilbert space and dense form domain ensure a nonempty set, bounded below by zero. The infimum need not be attained.
--   - `formEcdMagnitude`: PDF p.6: the exact channel-difference ECD expression for a GENERAL positive densely defined observable, including continuous spectrum. The accepted closed-form expectation equals the source spectral-cutoff energy.
--   - `DiscreteSpectrum`: PDF p.6, Proposition 3B: a COMPLETE eigenbasis, with eigenvalues counting multiplicity and with finite bounded sublevel sets. A countably infinite basis and finite sublevels express eigenvalues escaping to infinity.
--   - `StrongConvergence`: PDF pp.4,6: pointwise trace-norm convergence on EVERY normalized state.
--   - `formEcdTopology`: PDF p.6 footnote 3: topology generated by the actual ECD distances to all centers. On channels and E>ground these are finite metric distances.
--   - `constrainedChi`: PDF p.14, (19): actual constrained Holevo capacity. Reuse the accepted finite-ensemble definition. It equals the finite/countable supremum: grouping a countable tail into its barycenter preserves the entire average and energy, and the finite grouped Holevo informations increase to the countable value.
--   - `additiveBlockEnergy`: PDF pp.13–14, (17)–(18): actual additive n-use energy. For positive observables, the energy of the sum is the sum of the actual marginal energies, including infinity. This accepts every block state, including entangled states.
--   - `blockConstrainedChi`: PDF p.14: Holevo capacity of Phi^tensor n with additive energy bound nE. The complete n-fold coefficient space is used; no product-state restriction.
--   - `constrainedClassical`: PDF p.14: regularized classical capacity in nats per use. The source's limit exists; the extended liminf evaluates it without choosing a real value. Every positive block length occurs in the sequence; n=0 does not affect atTop.
--   - `perSiteConstrainedChi`: PDF pp.15–16: the comparison supremum with energy<=E on every single-site marginal of the computed ensemble BARYCENTER. Individual codewords are not constrained; no maximizing ensemble is chosen or assumed.
--   - `constrainedAssisted`: PDF pp.16–17: the actual entanglement-assisted capacity via the accepted supremum of channel QMI over energy-admissible states and genuine purifications.
--   - `FixedEnergyAmplification`: PDF pp.14,16, condition (21): finite amplification at ONE fixed input energy, for every admissible state. This is not global homogeneous control. Printed (21) omits Tr; the expected output energy here follows the explicit Tr expressions on p.16 and the energy definition. Correction review is pending.
--   - `CapacityUniformOn`: PDF p.18, corrected ECD-uniform interpretation: values are finite on the specified set, and one delta works for all pairs of its channels.
-- source:
--   Energy-constrained diamond norms and their use in quantum information theory, arXiv:1706.00361v2, https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.00361v2

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Dependency50_P33
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Frontier18_P01
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Frontier18_P08
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Claimed50_P32
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Claimed50_P35
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Claimed50_P13
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Claimed50_P39

/-!
Shirokov, arXiv:1706.00361v2. Seven retained nodes; all other nodes are
individually deferred in HARD.md/GAPS.json. Compilation is pending.
For Corollaries 1 and 2 both Hamiltonians have discrete spectra by their
hypotheses, so their infinite-dimensional separable spaces are expressed in
Hamiltonian eigenbases indexed by Nat, counting multiplicities. This coordinate
choice is exhaustive for those corollaries, but would restrict the other
propositions. The corollaries explicitly correct the source's arbitrary-metric
wording to uniform continuity for each specified ECD distance.
-/

noncomputable section

open Filter MeasureTheory
open scoped Topology ENNReal NNReal BigOperators

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Next46.P08

export QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P32 (StrongChannel)

export QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Frontier18.P07
  (GeneralizedEnsemble ensembleHolevo)

export QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P39 (g)

namespace Nuclear

export QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Dependency50.P33
  (State traceSize tensorApply productCoeff)

end Nuclear

namespace Entropic

export QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Frontier18.P01
  (generalizedRelativeEntropy)

end Entropic

namespace Marginal

export QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Frontier18.P08
  (partialTraceFirst partialTraceSecond)

end Marginal

/-- PDF pp.6,8: spectral-cutoff energy in a Hamiltonian eigenbasis, retaining
infinity. Used on positive nuclear coefficients, including actual marginals;
the nonnegative series equals the supremum of bounded spectral-cutoff traces. -/
def diagonalEnergy (energy : ℕ → ℝ≥0) (X : Matrix ℕ ℕ ℂ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∑' i, (energy i : ℝ≥0∞) * ENNReal.ofReal (X i i).re

/-- PDF p.6: spectrum infimum for an unordered nonnegative eigenvalue list; the
range is nonempty and bounded below by zero. The accepted Frontier30.P05
groundEnergy instead requires an ordered divergent EnergySpectrum. -/
def eigenbasisGroundEnergy (energy : ℕ → ℝ≥0) : ℝ :=
  sInf (Set.range (fun i => (energy i : ℝ)))

/-- PDF p.8, (6): every positive inverse temperature has finite partition
trace. In particular all spectral sublevel sets are finite. This series
adapter accepts an eigenvalue list; the accepted P13.GibbsCondition instead
accepts a general closed quadratic form and is used directly below. -/
def EigenbasisGibbsCondition (energy : ℕ → ℝ≥0) : Prop :=
  ∀ beta : ℝ, 0 < beta →
    (∑' i, ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (-beta * (energy i : ℝ)))) < ⊤

/-- PDF p.10: coefficients of the actual trace-norm Bochner barycenter.
State coordinates are bounded and trace-norm continuous, so these scalar
integrals are integrable and uniquely specify that same normalized state. -/
abbrev ensembleBarycenter (mu : GeneralizedEnsemble ℕ) : Matrix ℕ ℕ ℂ :=
  QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Frontier18.P07.averageCoefficients mu

/-- PDF p.6, (2): full channel-difference ECD supremum, without a half.
The reference is fixed, infinite-dimensional and separable. Every normalized,
possibly entangled, energy-admissible state occurs. On channel differences
this extended expression is finite (at most two); no real conversion is used. -/
def ecdMagnitude (energy : ℕ → ℝ≥0) (E : ℝ) (Phi Psi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨆ rho : {rho : Nuclear.State (ℕ × ℕ) //
    diagonalEnergy energy (Marginal.partialTraceSecond rho.coefficients) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal E},
    Nuclear.traceSize (Nuclear.tensorApply Phi.val.act rho.val.coefficients -
      Nuclear.tensorApply Psi.val.act rho.val.coefficients)

/-- PDF pp.12–13: trace out every site except k. Configurations fixed to zero
at k index exactly the discarded coordinates; updating to i,j inserts the
retained matrix indices. No finite-support restriction is imposed. -/
def siteMarginal {n : ℕ} (k : Fin n)
    (X : Matrix (Fin n → ℕ) (Fin n → ℕ) ℂ) : Matrix ℕ ℕ ℂ :=
  fun i j => ∑' a : {a : Fin n → ℕ // a k = 0},
    X (Function.update a.val k i) (Function.update a.val k j)

/-- PDF p.12: computed maximum of actual input marginal energies.
The empty extended supremum is zero; block statements require n>=1. -/
def maxInputEnergy {n : ℕ} {C : Type} (energy : ℕ → ℝ≥0)
    (rho : Nuclear.State ((Fin n → ℕ) × C)) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨆ k : Fin n, diagonalEnergy energy
    (siteMarginal k (Marginal.partialTraceSecond rho.coefficients))

/-- PDF p.13: computed MEAN output energy, using actual input marginals. -/
def meanOutputEnergy {n : ℕ} {C : Type} (energy : ℕ → ℝ≥0)
    (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ) (rho : Nuclear.State ((Fin n → ℕ) × C)) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  (n : ℝ≥0∞)⁻¹ * ∑ k : Fin n, diagonalEnergy energy
    (Phi.val.act (siteMarginal k (Marginal.partialTraceSecond rho.coefficients)))

/-- PDF pp.12–13: actual memoryless n-copy output with reference untouched.
Reuse the accepted tensor power, including every off-diagonal block.
Claimed50.P40.blockOutput instead constructs finite classical-input product
states; it cannot evaluate arbitrary entangled inputs or an untouched reference. -/
def referencedTensorOutput {n : ℕ} {C : Type} (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ)
    (rho : Nuclear.State ((Fin n → ℕ) × C)) :
    Matrix ((Fin n → ℕ) × C) ((Fin n → ℕ) × C) ℂ :=
  Nuclear.tensorApply
    (QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P35.traceClassChannelPower Phi.val.act n)
    rho.coefficients

/-- PDF p.4, (1), and p.13: extended block QMI as relative entropy with its
actual marginals, avoiding subtraction of possibly infinite entropies. -/
def blockMutualInformation {n : ℕ} {C : Type} (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ)
    (rho : Nuclear.State ((Fin n → ℕ) × C)) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  let X := referencedTensorOutput Phi rho
  Entropic.generalizedRelativeEntropy X
    (Nuclear.productCoeff (Marginal.partialTraceSecond X) (Marginal.partialTraceFirst X))

/-- PDF p.10: r_epsilon(t), used at epsilon>0 and 0<t<=1/(2epsilon).
The denominator is at least one half on this domain. -/
def continuityRatio (epsilon t : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  (1 + t / 2) / (1 - epsilon * t)

/-- PDF p.10, (12): the complete scalar Holevo continuity expression. -/
def holevoBound (F : ℝ → ℝ) (E epsilon t : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  epsilon * (2 * t + continuityRatio epsilon t) * F (E / (epsilon * t)) +
    2 * g (epsilon * continuityRatio epsilon t) +
    2 * Real.binEntropy (epsilon * t)

/-- PDF pp.8–9, (9)–(10): scalar regularity of a majorant, without imposing
continuity of the second derivative. Domination of F_H is irrelevant to
Remark 2's scalar implication from (10). -/
def MajorantRegularity (F : ℝ → ℝ) : Prop :=
  DifferentiableOn ℝ F (Set.Ioi 0) ∧
  DifferentiableOn ℝ (deriv F) (Set.Ioi 0) ∧
  (∀ x : ℝ, 0 < x → 0 < F x ∧ 0 < deriv F x ∧ deriv (deriv F) x < 0) ∧
  Asymptotics.IsLittleO atTop F (fun x : ℝ => x)

example (energy : ℕ → ℝ≥0) : diagonalEnergy energy 0 = 0 := by
  simp [diagonalEnergy]

example : eigenbasisGroundEnergy (fun _ => 0) = 0 := by
  simp [eigenbasisGroundEnergy]

example : g 0 = 0 := by
  simp [g]

example (epsilon : ℝ) : continuityRatio epsilon 0 = 1 := by
  simp [continuityRatio]

example (F : ℝ → ℝ) (E : ℝ) : holevoBound F E 0 1 = 0 := by
  simp [holevoBound, g]

example {n : ℕ} (k : Fin n) :
    siteMarginal k (0 : Matrix (Fin n → ℕ) (Fin n → ℕ) ℂ) = 0 := by
  funext i j
  simp [siteMarginal]

example (energy : ℕ → ℝ≥0) (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ) (rho : Nuclear.State ((Fin 0 → ℕ) × Unit)) :
    maxInputEnergy energy rho = 0 ∧ meanOutputEnergy energy Phi rho = 0 := by
  simp [maxInputEnergy, meanOutputEnergy]

namespace Forms

export QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P13
  (PositiveObservable closedFormExpectation)

end Forms

/-- PDF pp.5–6: spectral infimum via the equivalent Rayleigh infimum on the
unit form domain. A nonzero separable Hilbert space and dense form domain
ensure a nonempty set, bounded below by zero. The infimum need not be attained. -/
def formGroundEnergy {I : Type} (H : Forms.PositiveObservable I) : ℝ :=
  sInf {v : ℝ | ∃ u : QAlgorithms.RealRegisters.Hilbert I,
    ‖u‖ = 1 ∧ H.form u < ⊤ ∧ v = (H.form u).toReal}

/-- PDF p.6: the exact channel-difference ECD expression for a GENERAL
positive densely defined observable, including continuous spectrum. The
accepted closed-form expectation equals the source spectral-cutoff energy. -/
def formEcdMagnitude {I J : Type} (H : Forms.PositiveObservable I) (E : ℝ)
    (Phi Psi : QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P32.StrongChannel I J) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨆ rho : {rho : Nuclear.State (I × ℕ) //
    Forms.closedFormExpectation H (Marginal.partialTraceSecond rho.coefficients) ≤
      ENNReal.ofReal E},
    Nuclear.traceSize (Nuclear.tensorApply Phi.val.act rho.val.coefficients -
      Nuclear.tensorApply Psi.val.act rho.val.coefficients)

/-- PDF p.6, Proposition 3B: a COMPLETE eigenbasis, with eigenvalues counting
multiplicity and with finite bounded sublevel sets. A countably infinite basis
and finite sublevels express eigenvalues escaping to infinity. -/
def DiscreteSpectrum {I : Type} (H : Forms.PositiveObservable I) : Prop :=
  ∃ (b : HilbertBasis ℕ ℂ (QAlgorithms.RealRegisters.Hilbert I))
    (energy : ℕ → ℝ≥0),
    QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P32.IsEnergyOperator energy ∧
    ∀ u, H.form u = ∑' k, (energy k : ℝ≥0∞) *
      ENNReal.ofReal (‖inner ℂ (b k) u‖ ^ 2)

/-- PDF pp.4,6: pointwise trace-norm convergence on EVERY normalized state. -/
def StrongConvergence {I J : Type}
    (seq : ℕ → QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P32.StrongChannel I J)
    (Phi : QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P32.StrongChannel I J) : Prop :=
  ∀ rho : Nuclear.State I,
    Tendsto (fun n => Nuclear.traceSize
      ((seq n).val.act rho.coefficients - Phi.val.act rho.coefficients)) atTop (nhds 0)

/-- PDF p.6 footnote 3: topology generated by the actual ECD distances to
all centers. On channels and E>ground these are finite metric distances. -/
def formEcdTopology {I J : Type} (H : Forms.PositiveObservable I) (E : ℝ) :
    TopologicalSpace (QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P32.StrongChannel I J) :=
  TopologicalSpace.induced
    (fun Phi : QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P32.StrongChannel I J =>
      fun Psi : QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P32.StrongChannel I J =>
        formEcdMagnitude H E Phi Psi) inferInstance

/-- PDF p.14, (19): actual constrained Holevo capacity. Reuse the accepted
finite-ensemble definition. It equals the finite/countable supremum: grouping
a countable tail into its barycenter preserves the entire average and energy,
and the finite grouped Holevo informations increase to the countable value. -/
abbrev constrainedChi (H : Forms.PositiveObservable ℕ) (E : ℝ) (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P13.chiCapacity Phi.val.act H E

/-- PDF pp.13–14, (17)–(18): actual additive n-use energy. For positive
observables, the energy of the sum is the sum of the actual marginal energies,
including infinity. This accepts every block state, including entangled states. -/
def additiveBlockEnergy (H : Forms.PositiveObservable ℕ) (n : ℕ)
    (X : Matrix (Fin n → ℕ) (Fin n → ℕ) ℂ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∑ k : Fin n, Forms.closedFormExpectation H (siteMarginal k X)

/-- PDF p.14: Holevo capacity of Phi^tensor n with additive energy bound nE.
The complete n-fold coefficient space is used; no product-state restriction. -/
def blockConstrainedChi (H : Forms.PositiveObservable ℕ) (E : ℝ)
    (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ) (n : ℕ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Frontier18.P07.finiteEnsembleCapacity
    (QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P35.traceClassChannelPower Phi.val.act n)
    {rho | additiveBlockEnergy H n rho.coefficients ≤
      (n : ℝ≥0∞) * ENNReal.ofReal E}

/-- PDF p.14: regularized classical capacity in nats per use. The source's
limit exists; the extended liminf evaluates it without choosing a real value.
Every positive block length occurs in the sequence; n=0 does not affect atTop. -/
abbrev constrainedClassical (H : Forms.PositiveObservable ℕ) (E : ℝ)
    (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P13.regularizedUnassistedCapacity Phi.val.act H E

/-- PDF pp.15–16: the comparison supremum with energy<=E on every
single-site marginal of the computed ensemble BARYCENTER. Individual codewords
are not constrained; no maximizing ensemble is chosen or assumed. -/
def perSiteConstrainedChi (H : Forms.PositiveObservable ℕ) (E : ℝ)
    (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ) (n : ℕ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Frontier18.P07.finiteEnsembleCapacity
    (QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P35.traceClassChannelPower Phi.val.act n)
    {rho | ∀ k : Fin n, Forms.closedFormExpectation H (siteMarginal k rho.coefficients) ≤
      ENNReal.ofReal E}

example (H : Forms.PositiveObservable ℕ) (X : Matrix (Fin 0 → ℕ) (Fin 0 → ℕ) ℂ) :
    additiveBlockEnergy H 0 X = 0 := by
  simp [additiveBlockEnergy]

/-- PDF pp.16–17: the actual entanglement-assisted capacity via the accepted
supremum of channel QMI over energy-admissible states and genuine purifications. -/
abbrev constrainedAssisted (H : Forms.PositiveObservable ℕ) (E : ℝ) (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P13.informationSupremum Phi.val.act H E

/-- PDF pp.14,16, condition (21): finite amplification at ONE fixed input
energy, for every admissible state. This is not global homogeneous control.
Printed (21) omits Tr; the expected output energy here follows the explicit
Tr expressions on p.16 and the energy definition. Correction review is pending. -/
def FixedEnergyAmplification (HA HB : Forms.PositiveObservable ℕ) (E k : ℝ)
    (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ rho : Nuclear.State ℕ,
    Forms.closedFormExpectation HA rho.coefficients ≤ ENNReal.ofReal E →
      Forms.closedFormExpectation HB (Phi.val.act rho.coefficients) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (k * E)

/-- PDF p.18, corrected ECD-uniform interpretation: values are finite on the
specified set, and one delta works for all pairs of its channels. -/
def CapacityUniformOn (HA : Forms.PositiveObservable ℕ) (L : ℝ)
    (value : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ → ℝ≥0∞) (S : Set (StrongChannel ℕ ℕ)) : Prop :=
  (∀ Phi ∈ S, value Phi < ⊤) ∧
  ∀ eta : ℝ, 0 < eta → ∃ delta : ℝ, 0 < delta ∧
    ∀ Phi ∈ S, ∀ Psi ∈ S,
      formEcdMagnitude HA L Phi Psi < ENNReal.ofReal delta →
        |(value Phi).toReal - (value Psi).toReal| < eta

example (n : ℕ) (X : Matrix (Fin n → ℕ) (Fin n → ℕ) ℂ) :
    additiveBlockEnergy
      (QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P13.zeroObservable ℕ) n X = 0 := by
  simp [additiveBlockEnergy, QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P13.closedFormExpectation,
    QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P13.zeroObservable]

example (HA : Forms.PositiveObservable ℕ) (E k : ℝ) (Phi : StrongChannel ℕ ℕ) :
    FixedEnergyAmplification HA
      (QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P13.zeroObservable ℕ) E k Phi := by
  simp [FixedEnergyAmplification,
    QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P13.closedFormExpectation,
    QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P13.zeroObservable]

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Next46.P08


